WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:03.210
- The body of the dragon

00:00:04.496 --> 00:00:06.043
Oh, I'm so nervous!

00:00:06.487 --> 00:00:07.830
(Inga claps hands)

00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:09.042
Oh, I'm so nervous.

00:00:09.042 --> 00:00:12.125
(upbeat jazzy music)

00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:14.100
Hey guys, it's Inga.

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:16.050
So last time, I made Dragon's Beard candy.

00:00:16.050 --> 00:00:19.233
Today, I'm gonna try painting with sugar.

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:22.310
Sugar painting has been
around for centuries,

00:00:22.310 --> 00:00:25.140
it is this amazing art
form, where people use sugar

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:26.700
to paint different characters,

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:30.500
anything from rabbits,
to monkeys, to dragons.

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:32.050
When I was traveling around China,

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:33.930
I saw these artists on the streets,

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:36.380
and I thought it was
the most amazing thing.

00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:38.620
I am not really an artist,

00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:40.407
I don't even have a recipe for this, so,

00:00:40.407 --> 00:00:42.140
I'm just gonna be winging it.

00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:43.140
It's gonna be great.

00:00:43.297 --> 00:00:44.130
(Inga claps hands)
Sugar painting.

00:00:44.130 --> 00:00:44.990
First things first!

00:00:44.990 --> 00:00:45.823
I've no idea what sugar I'm gonna use,

00:00:45.823 --> 00:00:48.800
so I'm just going to
test out different types,

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:50.950
and different ratios.

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:52.775
For our first attempt, we're gonna go with

00:00:52.775 --> 00:00:56.420
one cup of rock sugar,
and one cup of water.

00:00:56.420 --> 00:00:58.649
I think I'm supposed to
boil the water first.

00:00:58.649 --> 00:01:00.460
(energetic music)

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:01.293
Here we go.

00:01:03.264 --> 00:01:04.097
(cellophane crinkles)

00:01:04.097 --> 00:01:05.210
I feel like we need a little bit more.

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:07.597
I'm supposed to continue stirring this.

00:01:07.597 --> 00:01:11.097
(dynamic repeating music)

00:01:13.290 --> 00:01:15.780
Now it's looking a lot stickier.

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:16.613
Do you see that?

00:01:16.613 --> 00:01:18.610
I hope it means I'm on the right track.

00:01:18.610 --> 00:01:20.240
Yeah, I'm gonna turn it down now.

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:22.840
I'm just wondering if it's
supposed to bubble this much.

00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:24.510
It doesn't look like the right color.

00:01:24.510 --> 00:01:25.820
Did I overcook it?

00:01:25.820 --> 00:01:27.217
Oh my God, it is crystallizing.

00:01:27.217 --> 00:01:28.180
(bell dings)

00:01:28.180 --> 00:01:29.253
I failed.

00:01:30.830 --> 00:01:32.200
Let's go for round two.

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:33.463
(swoosh)

00:01:33.470 --> 00:01:34.303
Round two.

00:01:34.303 --> 00:01:37.903
We are gonna do one cup of
sugar and two cups of water.

00:01:37.940 --> 00:01:38.773
Fingers crossed.

00:01:38.773 --> 00:01:40.247
I'm gonna go with white sugar this time.

00:01:40.247 --> 00:01:41.603
I'm not gonna stir it.

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:43.830
We'll see how that goes.

00:01:43.830 --> 00:01:48.030
So right now, we have
sticky, gooey looking liquid.

00:01:48.030 --> 00:01:49.930
It's not quite the right color,

00:01:49.930 --> 00:01:51.860
but it's better than our first attempt.

00:01:51.860 --> 00:01:55.443
It's somehow... I'll
put it into cold water,

00:01:57.772 --> 00:01:58.605
Oh, that's hot.

00:01:58.605 --> 00:01:59.438
Tastes good,

00:01:59.438 --> 00:02:00.510
but I don't think it's
what we're looking for.

00:02:00.510 --> 00:02:01.523
I can't really draw with this.

00:02:01.523 --> 00:02:04.159
This is not how it's supposed to be.

00:02:04.159 --> 00:02:05.250
(bell dings)

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:06.880
We have failed yet again.

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:09.160
I don't know what to
do to make this right.

00:02:09.160 --> 00:02:10.280
I don't know what I'm doing wrong.

00:02:10.280 --> 00:02:11.800
If I can't figure out this sugar,

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:12.890
how can I get to painting?

00:02:12.890 --> 00:02:14.090
We're gonna end it here,

00:02:14.740 --> 00:02:16.590
and try something different.

00:02:16.590 --> 00:02:17.490
Yeah we can cut.

00:02:17.490 --> 00:02:18.323
(beeping)

00:02:18.323 --> 00:02:21.191
I am freaking out right now,
because we were gonna give up

00:02:21.191 --> 00:02:24.570
for the day, and I cut all the cameras,

00:02:24.570 --> 00:02:25.800
so I'm on my phone right now,

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:27.090
but look at this!

00:02:27.583 --> 00:02:29.653
Look at this color!

00:02:29.950 --> 00:02:32.400
Oh my God, I am so excited right now.

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:33.990
One second, I'm gonna pour it out.

00:02:33.990 --> 00:02:35.683
Here we go, whoa!

00:02:36.865 --> 00:02:38.535
(jazzy music)

00:02:38.535 --> 00:02:40.470
Oh my God, this is gonna
be such a good shot.

00:02:40.470 --> 00:02:42.413
It's so beautiful!

00:02:43.566 --> 00:02:46.000
(metallic scraping)

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:47.000
Look at this

00:02:47.217 --> 00:02:48.520
(knife clinks on marble)

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:50.810
We're gonna break it apart, like

00:02:51.541 --> 00:02:52.860
(knife clinks on marble)

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:54.250
It tastes like what I had.

00:02:54.250 --> 00:02:56.683
I am so excited.

00:02:56.780 --> 00:02:58.893
So I broke them into little pieces,

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:00.490
you can see right there.

00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:03.740
And now I am going to
reset everything back up,

00:03:03.740 --> 00:03:04.993
clean all the dishes,

00:03:05.350 --> 00:03:06.900
and we're gonna start painting,

00:03:07.553 --> 00:03:08.386
yay!

00:03:08.386 --> 00:03:09.219
(whooshing)

00:03:09.219 --> 00:03:10.052
So we're rolling again.

00:03:10.214 --> 00:03:13.210
I have my sugar candy
bits in this Mason jar.

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:14.580
You could totally eat this as is.

00:03:14.580 --> 00:03:15.670
It smells really good.

00:03:15.670 --> 00:03:16.760
I'm just gonna melt it

00:03:16.760 --> 00:03:19.693
on low heat, this might take a while.

00:03:19.827 --> 00:03:22.910
(jazzy guitar music)

00:03:26.920 --> 00:03:29.193
Does it look like drawing consistency?

00:03:33.490 --> 00:03:35.860
I think so, I think we might be ready.

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:38.893
My main goal today, is to draw a dragon.

00:03:38.930 --> 00:03:41.373
That is like the ultimate goal.

00:03:41.566 --> 00:03:44.110
But, we're gonna have to
do some practicing first.

00:03:44.110 --> 00:03:46.683
I should probably start
with something easier.

00:03:47.010 --> 00:03:48.003
Let's try.

00:03:49.542 --> 00:03:52.920
(fast jazzy guitar music)

00:03:52.990 --> 00:03:55.393
This is me trying to draw a butterfly.

00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:57.800
That's the easiest thing I can think of.

00:03:58.758 --> 00:04:00.055
(Inge laughs)

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:01.970
This is a bad butterfly.

00:04:01.970 --> 00:04:03.730
I wanted to go from this to a dragon.,

00:04:03.730 --> 00:04:06.250
I think we're being very optimistic here.

00:04:06.250 --> 00:04:07.083
Uh.

00:04:07.424 --> 00:04:11.200
I know it's not much to
look at, but it's my first.

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:13.032
Please bear with me.

00:04:13.032 --> 00:04:14.959
(metal tapping)

00:04:14.959 --> 00:04:17.105
Ohh, this is the first of it's kind.

00:04:17.105 --> 00:04:19.719
This could belong to like MOMA, right?

00:04:19.719 --> 00:04:20.981
(whooshing)

00:04:21.190 --> 00:04:22.093
Let's do this.

00:04:23.070 --> 00:04:26.820
(fast cheerful guitar music)

00:04:30.380 --> 00:04:31.213
Yay.

00:04:41.800 --> 00:04:42.940
Oh my God, I'm so close,

00:04:42.940 --> 00:04:45.040
a little bit more, just a little bit more!

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:49.815
Okay this one looks a little
bit more like a butterfly.

00:04:49.815 --> 00:04:51.320
(hands clapping)

00:04:51.320 --> 00:04:52.223
I'm scared.

00:04:54.136 --> 00:04:55.247
(metallic scraping)

00:04:55.247 --> 00:04:56.080
Oh!

00:04:58.887 --> 00:05:00.554
What's the best way?

00:05:00.693 --> 00:05:01.526
Oh!

00:05:02.949 --> 00:05:05.449
Does it look like a butterfly?

00:05:07.251 --> 00:05:08.823
We're slowly getting there.

00:05:09.509 --> 00:05:10.653
This is so stressful.

00:05:10.726 --> 00:05:11.559
(whooshing)

00:05:11.559 --> 00:05:15.290
It is about time for me
to really go out there

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:18.053
and do the dragon.

00:05:18.316 --> 00:05:19.149
(slow trumpet music)

00:05:19.149 --> 00:05:19.982
Only got one shot,

00:05:19.982 --> 00:05:21.553
so, let's try.

00:05:22.146 --> 00:05:26.479
(dramatic ominous orchestral music)

00:05:33.434 --> 00:05:35.123
Oh, I'm so nervous.

00:05:35.503 --> 00:05:37.452
(hands clapping)

00:05:37.452 --> 00:05:38.423
Oh, I'm so nervous!

00:05:46.231 --> 00:05:47.064
(metallic scraping)

00:05:47.064 --> 00:05:47.897
Come on!

00:05:48.193 --> 00:05:50.930
(dramatic percussive orchestral music)

00:05:50.930 --> 00:05:52.773
I don't even know if I can lift it up.

00:05:58.942 --> 00:05:59.775
Oh...oh.

00:06:01.080 --> 00:06:05.663
(dramatic choral and orchestral music)

00:06:12.188 --> 00:06:13.262
(gasping breath)

00:06:13.262 --> 00:06:15.200
So this is what we have so far,

00:06:15.200 --> 00:06:17.803
now the challenge is to pick it up.

00:06:17.870 --> 00:06:19.653
I am so nervous right now.

00:06:20.570 --> 00:06:22.170
I don't even know where to start

00:06:22.842 --> 00:06:24.507
(jazzy saxophone music)

00:06:24.507 --> 00:06:25.340
(metal clinks)

00:06:25.340 --> 00:06:26.457
(gasping breath)

00:06:26.457 --> 00:06:27.951
(laughing)

00:06:28.120 --> 00:06:29.923
Oh my God, oh my God!

00:06:34.350 --> 00:06:35.183
Here we go.

00:06:35.320 --> 00:06:36.320
It's all or nothing.

00:06:41.168 --> 00:06:42.659
(dramatic orchestral fanfare)

00:06:42.659 --> 00:06:43.492
Guys!

00:06:44.650 --> 00:06:46.113
I can't believe I did it!

00:06:46.580 --> 00:06:48.233
It's a friggin dragon.

00:06:48.940 --> 00:06:51.163
I'm like so scared I'm gonna drop it.

00:06:51.324 --> 00:06:54.574
(squeals with delight)

00:06:55.330 --> 00:06:58.730
I can't believe I actually did

00:06:58.760 --> 00:07:00.440
what I thought was impossible.

00:07:00.440 --> 00:07:03.240
I definitely burned the
sugar towards the end.

00:07:03.240 --> 00:07:05.770
Definitely a lot of room for improvement,

00:07:05.770 --> 00:07:07.943
but I'm pretty satisfied.

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:10.320
I would love to know what you
guys want me to make next.

00:07:10.320 --> 00:07:11.870
And see y'all next time.

00:07:11.870 --> 00:07:12.703
We did it!

00:07:15.275 --> 00:07:18.942
(upbeat jazzy guitar music)

